# Code ownership.
#
# This repository has one maintainer, @he8um. A single owner is declared for
# everything rather than inventing teams that do not exist -- an unroutable
# reviewer is worse than none, because GitHub will silently request review from
# nobody.
#
# What this file does and does not do
# -----------------------------------
# CODEOWNERS is INFORMATIONAL here. The `main` ruleset does NOT require code
# owner review, because with a solo maintainer that would make every pull
# request unmergeable: GitHub does not count a review from the pull request's
# own author, so the only person who could approve is the only person who
# cannot. The enforced controls are instead: pull requests are mandatory, the
# required status checks must pass, conversations must be resolved, and bypass
# is restricted. See docs/governance/repository-controls.md.
#
# The value it does provide: automatic review requests, an explicit record of
# which paths are sensitive, and a routing table that already works the moment a
# second maintainer exists.
#
# Later rules win in CODEOWNERS, so the catch-all is first and the sensitive
# paths follow.

# Everything.
*                                   @he8um

# Automation, release, and supply chain. A change here can publish an artifact
# or weaken a gate, so it is called out separately from ordinary source.
/.github/                           @he8um
/.github/workflows/                 @he8um
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @he8um
/.github/dependabot.yml             @he8um

# Security and support policy.
/SECURITY.md                        @he8um
/SUPPORT.md                         @he8um
/docs/security-model.md             @he8um
/docs/governance/                   @he8um

# Release records and runbooks. These are immutable historical evidence.
/docs/releases/                     @he8um

# The contracts and the Kernel: the deterministic core every surface derives
# from. Generated output under contracts/generated/ is owned with its generator.
/contracts/                         @he8um
/kernel/                            @he8um

# Architecture boundaries. The application layer is the shared use-case seam;
# the CLI and MCP server are presentation adapters over it.
/application/                       @he8um
/cli/                               @he8um
/mcp-server/                        @he8um
/runtime/                           @he8um
/planner/                           @he8um
/providers/                         @he8um
/skills/                            @he8um

# Persisted user data. The store format is a compatibility contract.
/project-memory/                    @he8um

# Installation, packaging, and distribution.
/installer/                         @he8um
/distribution/                      @he8um

# Build, validation, and release tooling.
/tools/                             @he8um

# The three machine-readable contracts that documentation and release
# qualification derive from.
